  "about": "Where Tools/ue_build_shed.py's grey-box kit gets its real models (Tools/ue_import_props.py dress(), run at the end of the shed build). Each swap spawns prop 'prop' (/Game/Shed/Props/<prop>/SM_<prop>) at 'at' (cm, the shed's frame; its floor point, or its wall point for wall kit) turned 'yaw' degrees (0: its front, +z in Torque Shed's frame, faces the shed's +y, the roller door; -90 faces +x, 90 faces -x, 180 faces -y), and hides the boxes labelled as in 'hide' (a trailing * matches every label starting so) in game and in the editor while keeping their collision, so walking, aiming and putting parts down behave exactly as before. A swap whose prop isn't imported leaves its boxes showing and says so in the log. A swap's 'prefer' list (all at its place) is used instead of its prop when every one of them is imported: a Fab model (Data/Props/fab.json) on our own shelf. 'dress' entries only add a model (no boxes hidden, no collision): the photoreal pass's clutter.",
